      "writtenOn": "2026-05-31T19:25:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like we are reading the same register we\u0027ve already read in iommu_pmu_counter_caps() above? We could avoid reading it 2nd time?\n\n(For example, we would avoid that if we read all these registers just once at pKVM initialization, similarly to the the host driver, per my other comment?)",
      "revId": "bc0e9123504f91f63878def0e58be942cb8e7d45",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0b2c983_5ba29639",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu_pmu.c",
