        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-31T19:25:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`num_ctrl` is capped at IOMMU_PMU_IDX_MAX in `iommu_pmu_num_counters()`, so we never have the `num_cntr \u003e BITS_PER_TYPE(u64)` case (otherwise we would need to support multiple PERFOVFSTS registers, per above)? So `GENMASK_ULL(num_cntr - 1, 0)` covers all needed cases?\n\n...Besides, using `BITS_PER_TYPE(u64)` instead of just 64 surely is an overkill? :)",
